[32m+[m[32mfor changes even though these modes do not use a source map.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mrnx-project session --manifest app/rnx.toml --no-splash --color=never[m
[32m+[m[32mrnx-project eval --verify --manifest app/rnx.toml -- '1 + 1'[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSession and eval accept `--verify` and `--color=auto|always|never` once, before[m
[32m+[m[32many `--` boundary, in either order with `--manifest`. Only session accepts[m
[32m+[m[32m`--no-splash`. Session takes no positional arguments or trailing `--`; eval takes[m
[32m+[m[32mexactly one source argument, including an empty string. `--offline` belongs only[m
[32m+[m[32mto lock/build. Run's existing script-argument boundary is unchanged.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll three launch modes share the receipt and source checks described below.[m
[32m+[m[32mThey inherit your working directory: relative CSV and Parquet paths refer to[m
[32m+[m[32mwhere you launched the command, not the manifest directory. Session loads your[m
[32m+[m[32musual rnx settings; eval does not. The executable owns the terminal, history,[m
[32m+[m[32msignals and exit status, with no proxy process. Reset clears bindings and retains[m
[32m+[m[32mextensions. Use a frame's `preview()` for bounded display; bare frames remain[m
[32m+[m[32mopaque. Opening a session releases the project command lock, and verification[m
[32m+[m[32mruns once before launch, not again between inputs. Rebuilding a project does not[m
[32m+[m[32mchange an already-running session.[m
